# 2. List map (bench/references.md §2), as the nearest Phase-1 program.
#
#   λf:Num -> Num. λxs:Num * Num. (f (fst xs), f (snd xs))
#
# Phase 1 has no lists and no pattern matching. A pair is the longest
# fixed-length sequence the type grammar can express, so `map` becomes map
# over a 2-element "list": apply f to both components. The shape of the
# reference program — take a function, take a container, rebuild the
# container with the function applied to each element — survives intact.

# λf:Num -> Num. ⦇⦈
construct-lam
move-parent
rename x0
set-ann Num -> Num
move-child 0

# λxs:Num * Num. ⦇⦈
construct-lam
move-parent
rename x1
set-ann Num * Num
move-child 0

# (f (fst xs), ⦇⦈)
construct-pair
construct-var x0
construct-ap
construct-proj fst
construct-var x1

# (..., f (snd xs))
move-parent
move-parent
move-next-sibling
construct-var x0
construct-ap
construct-proj snd
construct-var x1
